<dir>/cache.yaml: line 27: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 31: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 38: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 77: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 82: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 86: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 93: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 105: replace TODO
<dir>/cache.yaml: line 118: replace TODO
! invalid: 10 problem(s) in 1 definition(s) checked
! hint: fix the files listed and run 'jailops app validate' again; docs/apps.md has the format
[exit 2]

$ jailops app export cache -o <dir>/cache.yaml
! already_exists: <dir>/cache.yaml exists
! hint: keep it, or write over it with --force
[exit 5]

$ jailops app export cache -o <dir>/other.yaml
Wrote <dir>/other.yaml, drafted from jail cache, with 10 line(s) marked TODO.
The definition is named cache: rename the file to cache.yaml, or change name: to match the file name.
Next: fill in the marked lines and run 'jailops app validate <dir>/other.yaml'.

$ jailops app export cache --output <dir>/cache.yaml --force -q

